        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): block loopback canvas navigation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an Android canvas navigation gap where a gateway-controlled `canvas.navigate` URL could load loopback services on the Android device, including through WebView-compatible URL forms or main-frame redirects.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAndroid now normalizes canvas navigation targets before loading them and falls back to the bundled canvas for loopback or malformed `http(s)` targets whose host cannot be safely extracted. The Canvas WebViewClient applies the same check to main-frame navigations and redirects so remote pages cannot redirect the canvas into device-local services.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid users keep normal remote canvas pages and bundled file canvases, while local-device loopback services are no longer reachable through the canvas surface. This does not add settings, migrations, release-flow changes, or provider behavior changes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- `cd apps/android; JAVA_HOME=\"F:\\Program Files\\Android\\Android Studio\\jbr\" ANDROID_HOME=\"F:\\Android\\Sdk\" ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=\"F:\\Android\\Sdk\" .\\gradlew.bat testPlayDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.node.CanvasControllerSnapshotParamsTest`\n- `cd apps/android; JAVA_HOME=\"F:\\Program Files\\Android\\Android Studio\\jbr\" ANDROID_HOME=\"F:\\Android\\Sdk\" ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=\"F:\\Android\\Sdk\" .\\gradlew.bat testThirdPartyDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.node.CanvasControllerSnapshotParamsTest`\n- `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode local --base origin/main`",
